#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Hold static/software-factory.pdf to its source, the way the white paper's is held.

This began as a one-line refusal of the spike's stand-in PDF, by its digest. That
caught exactly one wrong file: any other placeholder, a stale build, a draft or a
hand-edited PDF passed it. The reference architecture now has a source and a
build (`bin/build-pdf --paper software-factory`) with a provenance manifest, so
it gets the same proof as the white paper instead: bin/check-pdf-current, for
this paper.

Behaviour when the PDF is absent is unchanged — it passes. The site links the
PDF only through fileExists-guarded templates, so with no file there is no link.
A PDF that is present must have software-factory/pdf.provenance.json describing
it, every input recorded there must be unchanged, and it must not be a draft. The
manifest must also record this paper's own inputs — software-factory.md, every
figure it references, the files that render it and the fonts it embeds — which
are computed from the tree, not taken from the manifest: the white paper built to
this paper's paths had a manifest that matched itself perfectly and passed here.
The stand-in has no manifest, so it is refused like any other unexplained file.
"""
import os, pathlib, sys

check = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().with_name("check-pdf-current")
os.execv(sys.executable, [sys.executable, str(check), "--paper", "software-factory"])
